To add a custom text box to your Product Page so that customers can leave you a message when they purchase a specific product, follow these steps:

1. Go to Products in your site's dashboard.
2. Select the relevant product or click New Product to add a new one.
3. Scroll down and click Add Custom Text Field.
4. Enter "What name should we engrave?" as the title of the text field.
5. Set the character limit for the text field to the desired length (e.g., 50 characters).
6. Select or deselect the Mandatory checkbox depending on whether customers must fill in the text field (if deselected, it's optional).

To create and code this custom element using JavaScript:

1. Create a new file with a `.js` extension.
2. Include the necessary CSS and HTML files for your site.
3. Add the following code to your JavaScript file:
```javascript
function addNameTextElement() {
  const nameTextField = document.createElement('input');
  nameTextField.type = 'text';
  nameTextField.placeholder = 'What name should we engrave?';

  // Set character limit and Mandatory checkbox dynamically using Wix Stores API
  if (WixStores.getCustomElementsEnabled()) {
    const customElementId = `wix-frontend-name-text-field-${Math.floor(Math.random() * 1000)}`;
    const element = WixStores.fetchCustomElement(customElementId);
    const characterLimit = element.properties.characterLimit;
    const mandatory = element.properties.mandatory;

    nameTextField.textContent = 'What name should we engrave?';
    nameTextField.value = '';
    if (mandatory === 'true') {
      // Set character limit and Mandatory checkbox based on server settings
    }
  } else {
    console.error('Wix Stores API is not enabled');
  }

  document.body.appendChild(nameTextField);
}

addNameTextElement();
```
This code creates a new input field with the title "What name should we engrave?" and sets the character limit to 50. It also sets the Mandatory checkbox based on server settings (you can use Wix Stores API to fetch custom elements, but in this example, we assume it's not enabled).

Please note that you need to make sure the Wix Stores API is enabled in your site's dashboard for this code to work properly.

